        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "The only clause is that the `habeas-requirements` skill \"MUST direct agents not to commit requirements or write implementation or test code until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group.\" It prescribes no library, algorithm, signature, type or delegation. The obligation is about what the skill document says. The supplied root, `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, is that document, so it is the artifact the clause applies to.\n\nThe root does carry the directive. In `section[Habeas%20requirements]/section[Workflow]`, step 4 has a **Gate:** \"no implementation or test code, and no commit, until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group.\" It adds that a general request to build the feature does not count as agreement. Step 5 (Commit) comes after that gate and commits only the agreed text, before any code. The wording matches the requirement's three outcomes (agreed, rejected, deferred) and both prohibitions (commit, and write implementation or test code). I found no structural gap and no missing root."
